    "text": "This is a greedy event-driven heuristic. The vehicle that becomes free earliest picks the unassigned, still-feasible ride with the best score, which is the ride's distance plus the bonus if it starts on time, minus the idle time before it starts. Each pick is O(N), so the total work is roughly (N + F) \u00d7 N, well within the limits. The output always has F lines with valid, non-repeated ride indices, so it meets the format rules. I have not run it against the actual data sets, so the score is untested.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Ride {\n    int a, b, x, y, s, f;\n    int d;\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int R, C, F, N, B;\n    long long T;\n    cin >> R >> C >> F >> N >> B >> T;\n    vector<Ride> rides(N);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        cin >> rides[i].a >> rides[i].b >> rides[i].x >> rides[i].y >> rides[i].s >> rides[i].f;\n        rides[i].d = abs(rides[i].x - rides[i].a) + abs(rides[i].y - rides[i].b);\n    }\n\n    vector<vector<int>> assigned(F);\n    vector<bool> used(N, false);\n\n    // Vehicle state: (free time, vehicle id). Position and time tracked separately.\n    vector<int> px(F, 0), py(F, 0);\n    vector<long long> ft(F, 0);\n\n    using Item = pair<long long, int>; // (time, vehicle)\n    priority_queue<Item, vector<Item>, greater<Item>> pq;\n    for (int v = 0; v < F; ++v) pq.push({0, v});\n\n    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        auto [t, v] = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n        int cx = px[v], cy = py[v];\n\n        long long bestKey = LLONG_MIN;\n        int best = -1;\n        long long bestStart = 0, bestFinish = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n            if (used[i]) continue;\n            const Ride &r = rides[i];\n            long long arrive = t + abs(cx - r.a) + abs(cy - r.b);\n            long long st = max(arrive, (long long)r.s);\n            long long fin = st + r.d;\n            if (fin > r.f) continue;\n            if (fin > T) continue;\n            long long gain = r.d + (st == r.s ? B : 0);\n            long long key = gain - (st - t);\n            if (key > bestKey) {\n                bestKey = key;\n                best = i;\n                bestStart = st;\n                bestFinish = fin;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (best < 0) continue; // vehicle retires\n\n        used[best] = true;\n        assigned[v].push_back(best);\n        px[v] = rides[best].x;\n        py[v] = rides[best].y;\n        ft[v] = bestFinish;\n        (void)bestStart;\n        pq.push({bestFinish, v});\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    out.reserve(1 << 20);\n    for (int v = 0; v < F; ++v) {\n        out += to_string(assigned[v].size());\n        for (int r : assigned[v]) {\n            out += ' ';\n            out += to_string(r);\n        }\n        out += '\\n';\n    }\n    cout << out;\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
